      "rev_n_1_356982_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_356982_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_356982",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through customers sequentially, maintaining a priority queue of available food types sorted by cost.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794531631.5358224
      },
      "rev_n_2_7d7def_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_7d7def_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_7d7def",
        "thought_text": "Use a hash map to track remaining dishes and a min-heap for efficient cost-based selection of food types.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794531631.535837
      },
      "rev_n_3_6d1b63_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_6d1b63_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_6d1b63",
        "thought_text": "Implement a greedy approach, always choosing the most cost-effective available option or the cheapest food type if none are available.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794531631.5358448
      },
      "rev_n_1_356982_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_356982_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_356982",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous implementation was that it didn't correctly handle the case where a customer orders more dishes than available of the requested type, but there are still dishes of other types available. The priority queue approach was correct, but the logic for serving from the cheapest available type needed to be adjusted to ensure it always serves the cheapest available dish, even if it's from a different type than requested.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_356982_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_453c985814",
        "created_at": 1794531731.4463263
      },
      "rev_n_2_7d7def_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_7d7def_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_7d7def",
        "thought_text": "The current approach using a min-heap for cost-based selection is inefficient for large inputs due to repeated heap operations. Instead, we can use a more optimized approach by maintaining a sorted list of available food types based on their cost and remaining quantity. This will reduce the time complexity and avoid TLE issues.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_7d7def_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_94a8ed0953",
        "created_at": 1794531772.0580385
      },
      "rev_n_3_6d1b63_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_6d1b63_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_6d1b63",
        "thought_text": "The current implementation has a logical error in the handling of the min-heap. The heap should be updated after each dish is served, not just when a new dish is added. This oversight causes the function to miss some dishes and potentially serve incorrect quantities of dishes.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_6d1b63_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_5bdc4ee879",
        "created_at": 1794531817.3758345
      },
      "rev_n_4_cccfb6_0": {
